  "decision_summary": "Most structurally similar analogs, especially beta-carbolines and related indole alkaloids, show direct brain uptake after systemic administration. The negative analogs are fewer and generally less similar or represent distinct chemotypes, so the overall evidence supports meaningful CNS access.",
